  m_Name: SQL_TYPE_08_UPDATE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: SQL_TYPE_08_UPDATE
  language: 3
  topic: UPDATE
  difficulty: 1
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Type the keyword that gives the room column its new value.
  code: 'Table: clues

    +----+----------+--------+

    | id | item     | room  
    |

    +----+----------+--------+

    |  1 | Backpack | Hall   |

    |  2 |
    Note     | Office |

    |  3 | Map      | Hall   |

    +----+----------+--------+


    UPDATE
    clues

    ____ room = ''Garage''

    WHERE item = ''Map'';'
  answerFormat: 1
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers:
  - SET
  caseSensitive: 0
  referenceFill: 
  runTests: []
  explanation: UPDATE table SET column = value changes existing rows. The WHERE part
    makes sure only the Map row is changed.
  hint: The keyword means 'put this value in the column'.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: A three-letter keyword comes between the table name and the
    column that changes.
